            <ArticleTitle>Aneurysm of the left main stem leading to anterior wall infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>51-3; discussion 53-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a woman with a spontaneous dissection of the left main stem leading to a large aneurysm compressing the left coronary artery. The lesion was initially treated with a conventional multicellular stent. However, persistence of the aneurysm required that two polytetrafluoroethylene-covered stents be implanted. Follow-up angiographic and clinical results were excellent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
